{"ticker":"AWL","symbol":"AWL","instrumentId":3178526,"name":"Awl Agri Business","industry":"NSE-Food-Packaged","about":"Adani Wilmar Ltd., a joint venture between the Adani Group and Wilmar Group, is one of India’s leading FMCG food companies, offering a wide range of essential kitchen commodities, including edible oil, wheat flour, rice, pulses, and sugar. The company’s flagship brand, \"Fortune,\" is India’s No. 1 edible oil brand. Leveraging the Adani Group’s local market expertise and Wilmar Group’s global sourcing capabilities, Adani Wilmar has become the largest importer of crude edible oil and a major player in the packaged food industry. With extensive manufacturing capabilities, including one of India's largest refineries in Mundra, the company also leads in industrial essentials like castor oil and oleochemicals.","website":"www.awl.in","location":null,"exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:06:00.047Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":171.19,"changePct":0.1990049751243801,"week52High":277.6,"week52Low":163.85},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹22,249 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹82,318 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"558,861,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"251"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"386,594,856"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.58%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"2.12"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.7"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"4.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.18"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.91"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"14%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"19.23"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"22–631"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"10.0%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"30.37"},{"label":"Volume","value":"1,727,918"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"2,186,428"},{"label":"Master score","value":"42"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"47"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"27"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"122"},{"label":"Acc/Dis ra